hadiths[count]{hadithnumber,text}:
"3033","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Wahb, narrated to us my uncle, who informed me Malik and al-Layth, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Sulayman ibn Yasar informed him that 'Abd Allah ibn 'Abbas informed him, who said:\n\nAl-Fadl ibn 'Abbas was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ). A woman from Khath'am came to the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) seeking his legal verdict. Al-Fadl began looking at her, and she began looking at him. The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) turned al-Fadl's face away with his hand to the other side.\n\nShe said, \"O Messenger of Allah, Allah's obligation of Hajj upon His servants has reached my father, an old man who cannot remain firm on the riding animal. May I perform Hajj on his behalf?\"\n\nHe (ﷺ) said, \"Yes.\"\n\nThis was during the Farewell Pilgrimage.\n\n---\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
